# Encrypted secrets backup configuration.
#
# Copy to config/backup-secrets.conf and edit. The real file is gitignored.
#
# scripts/backup-secrets.sh archives everything the admin panel needs that
# isn't ./data (accounts, API keys, session/signing secrets, tunnel and
# playit credentials) and encrypts it with age (https://age-encryption.org)
# against a public recipient key. The recipient key is safe to keep here, on
# the Pi: only the matching PRIVATE key can decrypt, and that key must never
# live on the Pi.
#
# One-time setup:
#   1. On a machine that is not the Pi: age-keygen -o secrets-key.txt
#   2. Keep secrets-key.txt off the Pi entirely -- a password manager or a
#      Mac keychain item, not this repo, not the backups/ directory.
#   3. Copy the "public key: age1..." line age-keygen printed into
#      AGE_RECIPIENT below, on the Pi.

# The age public key backups are encrypted against. Required; the backup is
# skipped with an error if this is unset.
AGE_RECIPIENT=""
